Use the graph of $y=\arctan x$ to explain its parity. Relate the points on the graph with inputs $1$ and $-1$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=13mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black,->] (-3.5,0)--(3.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-1.9)--(0,1.9) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,dashed] (-3.3,1.570796)--(3.3,1.570796);
\draw[black,dashed] (-3.3,-1.570796)--(3.3,-1.570796);
\path (-3.2,1.570796) node[above right,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$y=\frac{\pi}{2}$};
\path (3.2,-1.570796) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$y=-\frac{\pi}{2}$};
\draw[draw={rgb,255:red,38;green,140;blue,255},thick,<->,domain=-3.3:3.3,samples=100,variable=\t] plot ({\t},{rad(atan(\t))});
\foreach \a in {-1,1}{\draw[black] (\a,-0.05)--(\a,0.05);\path (\a,-0.05) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\a$};}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The graph of $f(x)=\arccos x$ is shown. Classify the function as odd, even or neither, and explain why its rotational symmetry does not make it odd. State $\arccos(-x)$ in terms of $\arccos x$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=22mm,y=13mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black,->] (-1.4,0)--(1.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-0.35)--(0,3.55) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[draw={rgb,255:red,38;green,140;blue,255},thick,domain=0:pi,samples=100,variable=\t] plot ({cos(deg(\t))},{\t});
\foreach \a in {-1,1}{\draw[black] (\a,-0.05)--(\a,0.05);\path (\a,-0.05) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\a$};}
\draw[black] (-0.035,1.570796)--(0.035,1.570796);
\path (-0.04,1.570796) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\frac{\pi}{2}$};
\draw[black] (-0.035,3.141593)--(0.035,3.141593);
\path (0.04,3.141593) node[right,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\pi$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Given $\arcsin\frac12=\frac{\pi}{6}$, $\arccos\frac12=\frac{\pi}{3}$ and $\arctan\frac1{\sqrt3}=\frac{\pi}{6}$:
(a) find $\arcsin\left(-\frac12\right)$, $\arccos\left(-\frac12\right)$ and $\arctan\left(-\frac1{\sqrt3}\right)$;
(b) determine the exact value of $3\arcsin\left(-\frac12\right)-\arccos\left(-\frac12\right)+\arcsin\frac12$.
